      "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/a/59ef9b/{size}.png",
      "created_at": "2014-11-17T17:30:00.000Z",
      "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"phantaskippy\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/phantaskippy/48/1897_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> phantaskippy:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>I ended up ruling that Smoke Bombs applied reduction immediately on redirection, so that Undaunted could not reduce the damage.</p>\n<p>I'm wondering if that was correct now.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Not according to my current understanding.&nbsp; While the different kinds of damage modification have a defined priority, the order <em>within</em> a category (e.g. Change Damage Amount) is up to the players.</p>",
