    {
      "id": 120763,
      "name": "phantaskippy",
      "username": "phantaskippy",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/phantaskippy/{size}/1897_2.png",
      "created_at": "2014-11-18T21:07:17.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>If you deal damage to multiple targets you get to choose the order, but if damage you deal causes response damage you cannot choose to continue the original damage before moving on to the new damage.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>What I wonder is if Smoke Bombs works like that, redirecting the damage causes a new reduction to trigger, whether that happens immediately or if it enters the stable of reductions and increases is the question.</p>",
      "post_number": 14,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T03:54:16.023Z",
      "reply_count": 0,
      "reply_to_post_number": null,
      "quote_count": 0,
      "incoming_link_count": 0,
      "reads": 0,
      "readers_count": 0,
      "score": 0.0,
      "yours": false,
      "topic_id": 11555,
      "topic_slug": "double-undaunted",
      "display_username": "phantaskippy",
      "primary_group_name": "playtesters",
      "flair_name": "playtesters",
      "flair_url": "/uploads/default/original/1X/f46928191dbf93b4d0df24571543f49779579225.png",
      "flair_bg_color": "",
      "flair_color": "",
      "flair_group_id": 41,
      "badges_granted": [],
      "version": 1,
      "can_edit": false,
      "can_delete": false,
      "can_recover": false,
      "can_see_hidden_post": false,
      "can_wiki": false,
      "read": false,
      "user_title": null,
      "bookmarked": false,
      "raw": "<p>If you deal damage to multiple targets you get to choose the order, but if damage you deal causes response damage you cannot choose to continue the original damage before moving on to the new damage.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>What I wonder is if Smoke Bombs works like that, redirecting the damage causes a new reduction to trigger, whether that happens immediately or if it enters the stable of reductions and increases is the question.</p>",
